2026-08-12 — implementation record

The RFC and implementation plan are immutable normative inputs. The cutover manifest is the
literal deletion inventory; this file records implementation progress and unresolved risks without
duplicating deleted protocol names.

The preflight commit recorded the two supported entry-point capability inventory, immutable
binding inventory, context ownership table, outer capacity envelope, durability profile, scope/
epoch rotation rule, and the typed ABI spike. The first implementation commit then established
the target package graph, singular fixed-tenant facade, State/Match-only Program shape, three-family
journal, Store-owned reduction, Runtime-owned affine execution owners, strict replay, EVM/Portfolio
value cutover, PostgreSQL mechanical boundary, and thread-affine keystore.

Current implementation status:

- Program, Capabilities, Journal, Store, Runtime, Replay, App, domains, adapters, and storage all
  compile in the default Nix shell.
- Store now validates exact selected preparations, replacement ordinals, direct State/Match
  continuity, fact request/selection parity, atomic conclusion candidates, object reachability,
  recursive heads, and bounded append capacity.
- Runtime now exposes call-correlated outcome, integrity-blocked, and unresolved access owners;
  only a direct-new preparation can produce a committed call. Assembly registration retains typed
  Pure/Access implementations and exact binding identities before a facade is created.
- EVM ingress converts malformed, unauthenticated, and ambiguous provider outcomes into the
  unresolved owner and bounds derived request/evidence values. Portfolio and EVM cumulative
  continuations validate declaration order, remaining work, asset Match payloads, and public
  integer-scaled results.
- Facts now carry an optional producer frontier and require selected completeness to attest the
  captured frontier. Configuration revisions have strict content identities, bounded affine
  writers, duplicate-request promotion, retained-prefix loading, and Memory/PostgreSQL parity
  surfaces.
- PostgreSQL loads verify run heads, frame digests, dense fact publication coordinates, selected
  publication references, and complete configuration prefixes before Store qualification.
- The manifest scanner is part of the Nix task graph and is required by the composite gate.

Latest audit hardening:

- The Store Match regression now proves that a selected payload can be the complete State input
  while the conclusion returns a distinct output; conclusion closure contains only reachable
  objects, while preparation closure retains the exact recorded input object.
- Runtime contains Pure evaluation, Access preparation, adapter construction, and future-poll
