Architectural decision and ordered commits

The dedicated architect review concluded that exact-head CAS, rather than a process lease,
coordinator, or production lock, owns same-epoch worker linearization. Raw backend conformance
proves mechanical outcomes; Runtime retains the separate provider-entry invariant. It also
required an executable capacity artifact with maximum fixtures, exact/+1 checks, and reservation
evidence. The resulting final continuation commits are:

- `1c025795` — `prove postgresql same-epoch process cas races`;
- `b8565fa4` — `record executable capacity envelope`; and
- `d8954209` — `measure runtime process memory high water`.

