Unrun or intentionally non-claims

No required implementation or verification task in the final Nixfied graph is unrun. The RFC/
plan explicitly admits no latency SLO, so no latency benchmark or threshold is claimed. Linux
`VmHWM` is diagnostic rather than a portable allocator contract. No failover, replica, quorum,
host-loss, or multi-primary test is claimed because `PrimaryCrashRestart` is the sole admitted
durability profile. The cross-process provider assertion is intentionally not simulated with a
fake external provider: backend CAS races plus Runtime's direct-new provider counter are the two
owner-specific proofs, and no provider credentials or raw responses enter tests or persistence.

Known limitations retained by the design

- trusted in-process Rust State, adapter, signer, and provider implementation code;
- provider factual trust remains an authenticated provider assertion, not independent chain truth;
- response-loss window before conclusion durability is neutral and may require owner parking;
- unproven mutating capabilities remain `EntryOnce`, so parked calls are not retried;
- cold resume and cumulative-context retention are bounded by the fixed run/frame envelope and may
  retain O(n²) canonical context bytes;
- binding replacement requires a new scope/writer epoch and old nonterminal runs are replay/read-
  only;
- there is no external rollback witness beyond the append-atomic Store/backend result; and
- only the two current EVM submission and Portfolio snapshot entry points are admitted.

Final deletion confirmation

No five-family branching, lane, join, collection, policy/credential/principal override, provider
authority, or old Program/spec/certification workflow definition, use, or identity survives in
product code outside explicit rejection/deletion manifests and narrow ordinary domain/tooling
words. Secrets are not logged, persisted, or returned by the new evidence, race, capacity, or
verification paths. The completion audit is recorded in this log; the RFC and implementation plan
remain untouched.

2026-08-13 — strict restore and identity audit continuation

Material uncertainties

