Implementation progress

- Replaced Store's generic JSON `ConfigurationRevision`/`ConfigurationSnapshot` and raw string
  preparation surface with `ResolvedConfiguration<C>`, opaque cloneable
  `ResolvedConfigurationHead`, affine `ConfigurationWriteSession<C>`, typed prepared append, and
  suspended unknown-acknowledgement owners. Each owner retains the exact Store opening; fields and
  affine constructors remain private and are covered by Trybuild contracts.
- Local `ValidatedConfig<C>` publication validates before Store entry, canonicalizes once, and
  performs zero decodes. External and retained ingress enforce the 16 MiB pre-allocation bound,
  strict canonical float-free JSON, secret rejection, exact `MfmConfig` schema and digest, one
  typed decode, and one domain validation. Direct commits promote the existing typed successor;
  `Found` verifies and ingresses the returned row; stale/conflict promote nothing; unknown
  acknowledgement retains the fixed physical id and owner.
- Kept the configuration stream globally ordered and heterogeneous. Typed restart load selects the
  latest matching schema at a captured global head, while its private CAS metadata carries that
  global sequence and cumulative bytes so the next successor does not reload or fold the stream.
  The persisted admission projection carries the selected revision's own sequence and typed
  content identity. Admission rechecks that both the selected and captured global coordinates are
  still retained before appending genesis.
